        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "A solution of Gd(acac)3·2H2O (0.05 mmol, 0.0247 g) in 20.0 mL of CH3CN and a CH2Cl2 solution (5.0 mL) containing HL (0.05 mmol, 0.0146 g) were mixed at room temperature. The mixture was stirred for 4 h at 70 °C and then cooled to room temperature. After filtration, the resulting solution was kept in the dark and concentrated slowly by evaporation at 4 °C. After about 7 days, block-shaped pale-yellow crystals of 1 were obtained.",
